[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":1797},["ShallowReactive",2],{"page-\u002Fdart\u002F01-introduction-and-setup":3},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":1790,"extension":1791,"meta":1792,"navigation":108,"path":1793,"seo":1794,"stem":1795,"__hash__":1796},"content\u002Fdart\u002F01-introduction-and-setup.md","Dart — Architecture, Compilation Pipeline & Toolchain",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":1774},"minimark",[9,13,18,22,273,277,415,532,693,700,940,948,1012,1016,1121,1125,1135,1199,1206,1396,1400,1457,1461,1589,1593,1596,1647,1650,1770],[10,11,5],"h1",{"id":12},"dart-architecture-compilation-pipeline-toolchain",[14,15,17],"h2",{"id":16},"compilation-pipeline-internals","Compilation Pipeline Internals",[19,20,21],"p",{},"Dart has three execution modes. Understanding the boundary between them is critical for debugging performance and behavioral differences across platforms.",[23,24,26],"code-wrapper",{"language":25},"dart",[27,28,32],"pre",{"className":29,"code":30,"language":25,"meta":31,"style":31},"language-dart shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","\u002F\u002F ── kernel snapshot (AST serialized, no machine code) ──\n\u002F\u002F Used by VM JIT: fast startup, interpreted or JIT-compiled at runtime.\n\u002F\u002F Pipeline: source → dart:_kernel (front-end) → .dill file\n\u002F\u002F\n\u002F\u002F ── AOT snapshot (precompiled to machine code) ──\n\u002F\u002F Used by Flutter release: no compiler at runtime, fast startup.\n\u002F\u002F Pipeline: source → kernel → TFA (tree-shaking) → machine code snapshot\n\u002F\u002F\n\u002F\u002F ── JIT (development) ──\n\u002F\u002F Source changes hot-reloaded via incremental kernel compilation.\n\u002F\u002F The VM compiles hot functions with an optimizing compiler (OSR).\n\n\u002F\u002F This program behaves differently in JIT vs AOT:\nvoid main() {\n  \u002F\u002F assert() runs in JIT (debug), stripped in AOT (release).\n  \u002F\u002F In release, the entire assertion body is dead-code-eliminated.\n  assert(() {\n    print('This print vanishes in AOT — no side effect in release.');\n    return true;\n  }());\n\n  \u002F\u002F In JIT, `DateTime.now()` in const context is rejected at compile time.\n  \u002F\u002F In AOT, tree-shaking removes unused const symbols entirely.\n  print('Running in ${const String.fromEnvironment('dart.vm.product', defaultValue: false) ? 'AOT' : 'JIT'} mode.');\n}\n","",[33,34,35,44,50,56,62,68,74,80,85,91,97,103,110,116,131,137,143,152,168,181,187,192,198,204,267],"code",{"__ignoreMap":31},[36,37,40],"span",{"class":38,"line":39},"line",1,[36,41,43],{"class":42},"sdCPZ","\u002F\u002F ── kernel snapshot (AST serialized, no machine code) ──\n",[36,45,47],{"class":38,"line":46},2,[36,48,49],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F Used by VM JIT: fast startup, interpreted or JIT-compiled at runtime.\n",[36,51,53],{"class":38,"line":52},3,[36,54,55],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F Pipeline: source → dart:_kernel (front-end) → .dill file\n",[36,57,59],{"class":38,"line":58},4,[36,60,61],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F\n",[36,63,65],{"class":38,"line":64},5,[36,66,67],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F ── AOT snapshot (precompiled to machine code) ──\n",[36,69,71],{"class":38,"line":70},6,[36,72,73],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F Used by Flutter release: no compiler at runtime, fast startup.\n",[36,75,77],{"class":38,"line":76},7,[36,78,79],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F Pipeline: source → kernel → TFA (tree-shaking) → machine code snapshot\n",[36,81,83],{"class":38,"line":82},8,[36,84,61],{"class":42},[36,86,88],{"class":38,"line":87},9,[36,89,90],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F ── JIT (development) ──\n",[36,92,94],{"class":38,"line":93},10,[36,95,96],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F Source changes hot-reloaded via incremental kernel compilation.\n",[36,98,100],{"class":38,"line":99},11,[36,101,102],{"class":42},"\u002F\u002F The VM compiles hot functions with an optimizing compiler (OSR).\n",[36,104,106],{"class":38,"line":105},12,[36,107,109],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":108},true,"\n",[36,111,113],{"class":38,"line":11